    "status": "approved",
    "summary": "Thesis §4.1: local index in redb, remote in any S3-compatible store, and immutability makes every cache layer trivially correct. This spec adds an ObjectStore over any S3-compatible endpoint through the object_store crate, with a hash-sharded key layout, outboard sidecars, and conditional puts for idempotency; an ObjectSource over the same endpoint so verified range fetches (015) work against remote objects; and a LayeredStore that reads through a local store to a remote one and writes through to both. Negative caching is forbidden by design: content is immutable, presence is not, so a miss is retried and never memoized.\n",
    "title": "Remote object backend: an S3-compatible store and the layered read-through cache"
  },
